# Testing

- Test behavior and public contracts, not private helpers or call counts.
- One behavior per test, named `test_<unit>_<behavior>[_when_<condition>]`.
  Parametrize instead of copy-pasting cases.
- Unit tests never touch the network, a real LLM, or the real clock. Fake at the
  boundary (the LLM client), not deep inside the code under test. Small checked-in
  fixtures are fine; writes go to `tmp_path`.
- Anything that needs an external service is an integration test, excluded from the
  local gate.
- Test work follows feature work: one end-to-end check per vertical slice, then focused
  tests for high-risk logic, external boundaries, and regressions. Test count and
  coverage are not goals.
- A flaky test is a bug: fix or delete it, never add retries or sleeps.
